WEBVTT

00:07:29.397 --> 00:07:31.630
that you won't be secure
when they're not here,

00:07:31.663 --> 00:07:33.730
that you won't be able
to make enough money,

00:07:33.763 --> 00:07:35.930
that you won't be satisfied
for years to come,

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:37.397
and try to address those fears

00:07:37.430 --> 00:07:39.563
to communicate your values
to your parents.

00:07:39.563 --> 00:07:42.230
CSB: Yeah, that makes a lot of sense,

00:07:42.263 --> 00:07:45.363
especially with different cultures
and figuring all that out.

00:07:45.397 --> 00:07:47.597
So we have another question
from the audience.

00:07:47.597 --> 00:07:49.297
Let's bring that one up.

00:07:50.197 --> 00:07:53.197
"How do you recommend
that people address feelings of guilt

00:07:53.230 --> 00:07:54.963
tied to someone who is deceased?"

00:07:54.963 --> 00:07:56.563
From John Henderson.

00:07:57.097 --> 00:07:58.897
SKK: That's such a great question.

00:07:58.930 --> 00:08:01.397
You know what I see
in the immigrant community